        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Original title:",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " Soudni proces s R. Cern\u00ednem, F. Kinskym a K. Rohanem pro poslech zahranicniho rozhlasu",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Translation:",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " Trial of R. Cernin, F. Kinsky and K. Rohan for listening to foreign radio",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Summary",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Three Bohemian noblemen were prosecuted by the Nazi Special Court at the German Land Court in Prague (Fourth Chamber) on 28 March 1944. The charge was listening to foreign radio broadcasts, primarily the BBC, in violation of the Decree on Extraordinary Radio Measures of 1 September 1939.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Defendants",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "orderedList",
      "attrs": {
        "order": 1
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Rudolf Theobald Graf Czernin",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ", born 25 August 1904 in Dymokury, great landowner of Chudenice, protectorate member",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Franz Graf Kinsky",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ", born 11 May 1879 in Adler-Kosteletz, great landowner, protectorate member",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Charles Viktor Prinz de Rohan",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ", born 26 June 1894 in Folkestone, English national",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "All three were detained at Prag-Pankratz, the notorious Nazi prison in Prague.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Sentences",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Count Czernin:",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " 3 years and 1 month penitentiary, 4 years loss of civil rights. Listening since the beginning of the war (1939). 7 months pre-trial detention credited.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Count Kinsky:",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " 2 years and 1 month prison, 3 years loss of civil rights. Listening since spring 1940. 4 months credited.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Prince Rohan:",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " 2 years and 1 month prison, 2 years loss of civil rights. Listening since November 1942. 4 months credited.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "All three radios confiscated.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Key Details From the File",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The case was handled at the highest levels of the Nazi occupation government. SS-Obergruppenfuehrer Karl Hermann Frank, State Minister for Bohemia and Moravia, was personally briefed on the proceedings.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Countess Czernin intervened on behalf of the prisoners. SS-Standartenfuehrer Dr. Gies responded to her letter (page 25).",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Count Franz Kinsky confirmed Count Czernin's statements during interrogation and admitted to listening to foreign channels (pages 20, 22).",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Reichsprotektor Dr. Frick himself took a personal interest in the case, with correspondence regarding the prisoners' welfare and the question of potential release (page 20).",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Kinsky was examined by the police chief physician at the Reichsprotektor's request (page 22).",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Relationship to Alexander Czernin",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Rudolf Theobald Czernin and Alexander Friedrich Czernin (born 1913) both belong to the Vinohrady/Dymokury line of the Czernin family, descended from Otakar Evzen Czernin (1809-1886).",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Rudolf's father, Depolt Josef Czernin (1871-1931), and Alexander's father, Pavel Bedrich Czernin (1879-1938), were first cousins. Rudolf and Alexander were therefore first cousins once removed.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Lineage",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Otakar Evzen Czernin",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "strong"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " (1809-1886)",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Depolt Theobald Czernin",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " (1836-1893) then Depolt Josef Czernin (1871-1931) then ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Rudolf Depolt Czernin (1904-1984)",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " convicted in this trial, and Humprecht Czernin (1909-1944) died at sanatorium Ples near Prague.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Pavel Bedrich Czernin",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " (1879-1938) then ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Alexander Friedrich Czernin",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " (1913) then Alexandra Czernin (1951) married Richard Fishlock.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Rudolf's brother Humprecht Czernin (born 9 February 1909) died on 19 September 1944 at the sanatorium Ples near Prague, during the height of Nazi persecution and under circumstances consistent with the regime's treatment of political prisoners.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Relevance to Section 58",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "This document provides direct evidence of Nazi persecution of the Czernin family in the Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia:",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Criminal prosecution under Nazi emergency decrees",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Imprisonment at Prag-Pankratz",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Deprivation of civil rights for up to four years",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Confiscation of property",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The offence, listening to the BBC, constituted a form of political resistance to the Nazi regime",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "version": 1
}